<div class="panel active" id="panel-engine">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:#9b59b6">Diagram 1 · Miasma RSR Pelton Array Engine — Phase 25</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">36 Pelton Wheels · 6 Cylinder Shafts · Two Spider Ladder Manifolds · 1,200 HP · 10,000+ RPM · Rear Mid Engine</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The <strong style="color:#9b59b6">Miasma RSR Pelton Array Engine</strong> is the heart of the Lamborghini Enkidu RSR.
    Six cylinder shafts sit transverse in the rear engine bay. Each shaft carries six Pelton wheels — 36 total across the full array.
    The Pelton wheel is the most efficient hydraulic turbine geometry ever designed — a double scoop cup with a center ridge splits incoming steam, deflects it through nearly 180 degrees, and extracts maximum momentum before exhaust steam clears the cup face.
    Two <strong style="color:#39a84a">spider ladder manifolds</strong> arch over the array — the top manifold sits above the top row of three cylinder shafts, the middle manifold sits between the rows — both shoot steam <strong style="color:#39a84a">straight down</strong> with gravity assisting delivery and deflected exhaust steam falling away naturally after each cup impact.
    All six cylinder shaft outputs combine via a <strong style="color:#ff4500">serpentine chain belt</strong> into a single output sprocket.
    A <strong style="color:#8B6914">bevel gear set turns the output 90 degrees</strong> to align with the rear drivetrain — transmission development is the primary Phase 25 engineering task.
    No reciprocating mass anywhere. Pure rotation from zero RPM. <strong style="color:#e8a020">10,000+ RPM</strong> ceiling determined by bearing limits and material strength — not piston reversal physics.
    Steam source unchanged — <strong style="color:var(--aegis)">Aegis Boiler Mark 1</strong> carried forward entirely.
  </p>

